  "_comment": "USD per million tokens {in, out}. Only add prices you have verified from the provider's official pricing page (record it in _sources); models missing here get cost = null (never guessed). Freeze this file's git revision alongside published results. costOf() applies one flat rate per model: tiered prices (long-context surcharges, Haiku 5.5 above 100K-token prompts) use the base tier, which covers bench turns (~7-9k tokens each). Optional cacheRead / cacheWrite are the cache-hit and 5-minute cache-write rates; usage.tokensIn counts all input including cached tokens, and costOf() prices the cached part at these rates (input rate when absent). openai/gemini cache implicitly (no write charge); anthropic caches at explicit breakpoints set by the provider adapter. When a provider's base URL is overridden (BENCH_OPENAI_BASE_URL / BENCH_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL / BENCH_GEMINI_BASE_URL), costOf() returns null instead of these list prices.",
